From 7449c76bb06fd96f4e1b225c798f987994322773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:11:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Test and document the preconditioners of MFEM, KLU,
 OrthoSolver and MUMPS

MFEMSolversTest (sequential and parallel, and on a GPU when the tests on
the GPU are enabled) solves the Laplace equation with each smoother type,
the reorderings of BlockILU, UMFPack and KLU, then a second operator of
the same pattern; KLUSolver reports a singular matrix; OrthoSolver gives
a solution orthogonal to the constant vector on a problem with null flux
boundary conditions; invalid options are refused. SparseDirectSolversTest
checks the options of MUMPS, with a tolerance depending on the precision.
The generic test checks the placements of the new entries and no longer
skips the host entries of MFEM and SuiteSparse when hypre computes on a
GPU. LaplaceSystem gives a problem with null flux boundary conditions.

The user guide, the glossary, the page on the execution settings and the
release notes describe the new entries and options.
